speechtext:
Ye$. The best schemes
of dealing with unemployment are surely those tested by experience, and I am free to say that so far as I have been able to observe the situation these two schemes at least should be continued and possibly extended. Now as to relief generally, I am quite sure my right hon. friend will agree that broadly speaking there are only three directions in which we may proceed: 1, by direct relief contributions to the provinces;
2,	by provision for relief works to be carried out in conjunction with the provinces;
3,	by some system of agricultural re-establishment, if you will, which may be carried on by this government alone or in conjunction with the provinces. I think he will agree that these are the three directions-
